.TH GRID_HANDLE_INPUT 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
grid_handle_input \- Move the cursor with the arrows, WASD or the dpad; scroll with the mouse wheel; hovering the mouse over a visible cell selects it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqgrid.h\(dq
.BI "bool grid_handle_input(Grid *g, const Input *in);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move the cursor with the arrows, WASD or the dpad; scroll with the mouse wheel; hovering the mouse over a visible cell selects it. Call from the owning scene's handle_input. Nothing happens while the grid is empty.
.SH RETURN VALUE
true on the frame the selected item is activated: Enter, space, PAD_SOUTH, or a left click on a cell. The scene then acts on g\->selected (feed the cat, equip the item, open the level).
.SH MODULE
grid (src/engine/grid/grid.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grid_render (3),
.BR grid_hit (3),
.BR grid_move (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
